WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.110
- [Girl] Oh, he did it.

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:03.450
Oh, my.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.030
- These are some people of the internet,

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:07.020
wearing a Meta Quest 2 headset

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.940
and playing Richie's Plank Experience.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.580
A game where you jump off a virtual plank,

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.370
sometimes using a real plank
to make it seem more real.

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:18.537
This is me playing the same game.

00:00:18.537 --> 00:00:19.537
There we go.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:26.380
But unlike those others, I used a trick,

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.640
so I could avoid a similar feint.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.040
Let me do a quick pass through check.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:31.873
All right.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:39.030
Okay, so you bought one of
these, the Oculus Quest Two.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:43.428
The quest two, wait, the
Oculus, the Meta Quests Two,

00:00:43.428 --> 00:00:44.270
that's it.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:45.550
The meta quests two.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.451
Then you realize this thing is really fun

00:00:47.451 --> 00:00:51.740
but also pretty flawed and
hard to figure out sometimes.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.660
Mom, is it you?

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:55.640
Luckily there are some hidden settings

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.690
and things you can buy that can help

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.210
with some of those issues.

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:00.750
Here are eight tips for making

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.830
the Quest work better for you.

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:04.330
Strap in everyone.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.150
Number one, reset your direction.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.580
Sometimes you don't wanna
keep spinning around like this

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:13.090
to find the main menu or
center spot in a gamer app.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.930
So reset your view.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.373
Look straight ahead in the
direction you want your main menu

00:01:17.373 --> 00:01:19.900
or center of your app to appear

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:23.540
then press and hold the Oculus
button on right controller.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:25.540
You'll see the Oculus logo appear.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.540
Once the ring reaches all away around.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:30.740
The virtual world will
snap to your new center.

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:33.853
Number two, double tap to pass through.

00:01:33.853 --> 00:01:38.853
I want you to remember this,
furniture is the enemy of VR.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.840
That's why you should enable pass through,

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.740
a feature that gives you a camera view,

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.640
albeit in black and white
of your real surroundings

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:50.210
without taking your headset
off, go to quick settings,

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.410
then settings and select guardian.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.860
Toggle on double tap for
pass through shortcut.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:00.170
Now tap your finger
twice on either the left

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:01.650
or right side of the headset.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:04.320
And you'll instantly see the real world.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:07.190
Number three, take screenshots.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:08.700
Sure, in whatever app you're in,

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.280
you can back out to this menu here

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:13.210
and click take photo, but that's annoying.

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:14.640
Instead on your controller,

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.330
just hold down the Oculus button

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:17.860
and then hit the trigger.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.033
You'll easily be able to snap screenshots.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:24.240
Sadly, there's no button combo
for video screen recordings

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:27.940
like these, which brings
us to number four,

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:31.293
enable voice commands, go to settings.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.700
Then system, then voice commands,

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:40.110
enable in-app voice commands.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:41.760
And then the controller shortcut.

00:02:43.777 --> 00:02:46.200
Now you can double-press
on the Oculus button

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.550
and the mic will start
listening for a command.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.210
What time is it?

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:54.070
- [Oculus] It's 10:44 at night.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:55.320
- What's the weather?

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.710
- [Oculus] Right now in Jersey
city, it's clear and 32.

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:00.273
- You can also go to settings,

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:06.110
experimental features
and enable, Hey Facebook.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:11.820
Then you can just use the wake
phrase to give your command.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.874
Hey, Facebook, launch Beat Saber.

00:03:14.874 --> 00:03:17.480
(music plays)

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:20.430
Number five, turn on phone notifications.

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:22.440
This is not fun.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:25.180
So instead, get your
phone notifications sent

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.310
to your headset.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.420
Pair your headset to the Oculus app

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:29.470
on your phone.

00:03:29.470 --> 00:03:32.640
In the app, go to menu and then devices,

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:36.373
then phone notifications,
and then toggle it on.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.050
You can customize what phone
notifications now get delivered

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.380
to your headset.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:45.223
Number six, strap a battery to your head,

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.760
an hour or two of playing a game

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.963
or wandering around in some virtual space.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:53.930
And you'll see the
battery get into the red.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:55.280
Getting battery low,

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.250
but not if you wear one of these,

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.440
yes, that's a battery patch strapped

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:00.950
to the back of my head.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:03.780
This is the Kiwi Power Bang Fixing Strap.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:06.460
For $35, you get a short power cable

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:09.610
and this strap which has
space for a battery pack.

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:12.200
You have to BYOB, bring your own battery

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:15.350
or you can charge your phone this way.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:16.810
It's very cool.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:17.980
If you wanna go higher end

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.550
and I kind of suggest you do.

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:22.593
Get Meta's own $109 Elite Strap,

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.700
battery inside here.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.623
Number seven, make your
controllers rechargeable.

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:34.671
Sadly, the Quest two controllers
require AA batteries.

00:04:34.671 --> 00:04:37.800
You could, of course buy
rechargeable, AA batteries.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:41.660
Or you could go for Anker's
$99 fancy charging station

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.710
which has its own rechargeable batteries

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:45.270
and these special covers.

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:47.443
So you can just dock them to charge.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.740
Number eight, use your hands.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:54.690
You know what they say?

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.823
Your hands are your best controllers.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.010
Actually, nobody says that

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:03.810
but really using your
hands can be very handy

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:05.330
when you wanna do something quickly

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:08.070
and you don't wanna
fumble for the controller,

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:10.450
go to settings then hands

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:15.450
and controllers, toggle on hand-tracking.

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:19.240
There are a few gestures to master,

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:22.790
to select something, pinch,
to scroll, move your pinch

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.290
in the direction you wanna go.

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:29.740
I can look at my hands pinch here.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:31.680
It gets to some quick settings, like

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:35.170
It can be a bit janky, but when it works,

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:37.220
it's pretty cool and don't worry.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:39.940
You can easily switch
between hand and controllers.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:42.390
The system just picks up the right input.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:44.360
All right, go live the dream

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.260
and strap a bunch of electronics

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:47.823
and a big battery to your head.

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:51.930
I'm sure that is very good for all of us.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:55.300
I love my family. I love everybody.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.000
Thank you for watching this video.

